      "slug": "crocodile-stitch",
      "term": "Crocodile stitch",
      "definition": "Five trebles worked down one leg of a base stitch pair, then five more up the other leg, creating a scale or petal shape that overlaps the neighbouring scales."
    },
    {
      "slug": "base-v",
      "term": "Base V",
      "definition": "The pair of trebles in the foundation row that each crocodile scale wraps around. Each V supports one scale."
    },
