  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "crocodile-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "crocodile stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " accent blanket is 60 x 80 cm. Each scale wraps five trebles down one leg of a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "base-v"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "base V"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and five more up the other, forming an overlapping tile. The scales sit on a plain treble background."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chunky yarn on a 6 mm hook makes scales large enough to see clearly. The scale structure means the blanket is heavier than its size suggests. Total yardage is around 400 g chunky. This is a slow pattern to work; it takes longer per row than a plain treble blanket."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Chunky yarn",
              "qty": "400 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "6 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 scales x 3 rows = 10 x 10 cm in chunky with a 6 mm hook. Work a test swatch of two full scale rows before starting the blanket."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation row (base V row)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 61. Work *tr, ch 2, tr* into every 4th chain. This creates the base V pairs for the first scale row. (15 Vs.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Scale row"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 5 tr down the right leg of the first V (counting from the top). Rotate work. Work 5 tr up the left leg of the same V (back upward). One scale made. Sl st to the ch-2 space of the next V. Repeat for every V across the row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Second base row"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the scale row, work a new base V row offset by half a repeat, placing each new V over the sl st join between two scales below. This offsets the scale rows for a true tile pattern."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continuing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Alternate scale rows and offset base rows. Work until piece measures 80 cm (approximately 8 scale rows). Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Secure all tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The crocodile stitch forms a self-finished edge; no additional edging is needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash chunky wool cool. Dry flat. Machine wash acrylic 40 degrees; the scale structure holds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The bobble blanket is a more accessible raised-texture pattern at the same advanced level. Or try the puff stitch throw for a softer three-dimensional texture."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
